# Regenerated wrapper-verification artifacts (todo 1 of wrp-defects-and-tooling-fixes):
# the runners rewrite these in place, so tracking them produced dirty-worktree noise
# instead of evidence.  The enumerated rules that were added here for them are gone:
# the pre-existing `build/evidence/` rule above already ignores every path under that
# directory, so they added no protection (F2-3(a) correction, verified with
# `git check-ignore -v`).  Keep it that way — and never add a blanket `*.dbg`.
# Formerly enumerated here and now redundant (all covered by `build/evidence/`):
#   wv_vector_logs/, wrap-mxu-regression.txt, wrap-regression-summary.txt,
#   wrap-sfu-regression.txt, wrap-vec-regression.txt, wrap-vec-status.txt.
# Historical statics stay tracked (gitignore does not apply to tracked files):
#   wrap-bug005-result.txt, wrap-bug007-result.txt, wv-bug007-*.log.dbg,
#   wv_bug005_logs/*.dbg
# Two special cases, reconciled per F2-3(b)/(c):
#   - wrap-sfu-debug.txt — 0 writers in scripts/ + sim/regression/ (at HEAD and at
#     f1d9652): a one-off T2 debug capture, not a runner output -> restored to
#     tracked with `git add -f` (byte-identical to its pre-untrack blob).
#   - wrap-mxu-regression.RED-pre-RTL.txt — untracked-but-kept RED witness; ignored
#     via `build/evidence/` above and deliberately retained on disk (NOT tracked).

